  <div class="project">
    <div class="h">🛠️ Mini-Project 1: Hover Button Pack</div>
    <p>3 buttons banao, har ek ka alag GSAP-powered hover effect ho:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;button class="btn btn--scale"&gt;Scale&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="btn btn--glow"&gt;Glow&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="btn btn--wiggle"&gt;Wiggle&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">document.querySelectorAll(".btn").forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener("mouseenter", () => {
    gsap.to(btn, { scale: 1.08, duration: 0.3, ease: "back.out(2)" });
  });
  btn.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => {
    gsap.to(btn, { scale: 1, duration: 0.3, ease: "power2.out" });
  });
});</code></pre>
    <p><strong>Aapka task:</strong> <code>.btn--glow</code> implement karo (<code>boxShadow</code> ya <code>backgroundColor</code> animate karke) aur <code>.btn--wiggle</code> (<code>rotation</code> ko aage-peeche animate karo, small timeline ya <code>yoyo: true, repeat: 1</code> use karke).</p>
  </div>

  <hr>
  <h1 class="part">Part 2 — Core Mechanics</h1>

  <h2>2.1 Easing deep-dive</h2>
  <p>Easing sabse bada factor hai jo decide karta hai ki animation "cheap" feel karti hai ya "premium." Har ease (linear ko chhodkar) ke teen variants hote hain:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">ease: "power1.in"    // slow shuru hoke accelerate hota hai — jaise girti hui cheez
ease: "power1.out"   // fast shuru hoke decelerate hota hai — jaise ball rolling to a stop
ease: "power1.inOut" // slow → fast → slow — jaise car accelerate aur brake karti hai</code></pre>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Ease family</th><th>Feel</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>power1</code>→<code>power4</code></td><td>Acceleration ki increasing intensity</td><td>General purpose UI motion (<code>power2.out</code> most common default)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>back</code></td><td>Overshoot karke settle hota hai</td><td>Playful pop-ins, <code>back.out(1.7)</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>elastic</code></td><td>Springy overshoot with oscillation</td><td>Bouncy, toy-like UI</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>bounce</code></td><td>Literal bounce, ball jaisa</td><td>Physical/cartoon effects</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>circ</code></td><td>Sharp, circular acceleration curve</td><td>Dramatic reveals</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>expo</code></td><td>Bahut fast start/end</td><td>High-energy motion</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>sine</code></td><td>Gentle, smooth</td><td>Subtle looping/breathing animations</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>linear</code></td><td>Constant speed</td><td>Rotating loaders, progress bars</td></tr>
  </table>

  <pre><code class="language-javascript">gsap.to(".box", { x: 300, ease: "back.out(1.7)" });   // 1.7 = overshoot strength
gsap.to(".box", { x: 300, ease: "elastic.out(1, 0.3)" }); // (amplitude, period)</code></pre>

  <p>Fully custom curves ke liye <code>CustomEase</code> load karo (ye bhi ab free hai):</p>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">import { CustomEase } from "gsap/CustomEase";
gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);

CustomEase.create("myEase", "M0,0 C0.126,0.382 0.282,0.674 0.44,0.822 0.632,1.002 0.818,1 1,1");
gsap.to(".box", { x: 300, ease: "myEase" });</code></pre>

  <div class="callout tip">💡 <strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> 90% UI motion ke liye <code>power2.out</code> ya <code>power3.out</code> use karo. <code>back</code>/<code>elastic</code> kam use karo — overuse site ko gimmicky feel karati hai.</div>

  <h2>2.2 Stagger</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">// Simple: har element ke beech 0.1s
gsap.from(".card", { opacity: 0, y: 40, stagger: 0.1 });</code></pre>

  <pre><code class="language-javascript">gsap.from(".card", {
  opacity: 0,
  y: 40,
  stagger: {
    each: 0.08,
    from: "center",     // "start" | "end" | "center" | "edges" | "random" | index
    grid: "auto",        // 2D stagger ke liye grid auto-detect
    ease: "power2.inOut"
  }
});</code></pre>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Property</th><th>Kya karta hai</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>each</code></td><td>har element ke start ke beech seconds</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td>sabhi elements mein spread total seconds</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>from</code></td><td>wave kaha se originate hoti hai</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>grid</code></td><td><code>[rows, cols]</code> ya <code>"auto"</code> 2D staggers ke liye</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>axis</code></td><td>stagger direction ko <code>"x"</code> ya <code>"y"</code> tak limit karo</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>2.3 Timelines - real power tool</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">const tl = gsap.timeline({ defaults: { duration: 0.6, ease: "power2.out" } });

tl.from(".hero-title", { opacity: 0, y: 40 })
  .from(".hero-subtitle", { opacity: 0, y: 20 })
  .from(".hero-cta", { opacity: 0, scale: 0.8 })
  .from(".hero-image", { opacity: 0, x: 60 }, "-=0.4");</code></pre>

  <h2>2.4 Position parameter - sequencing superpower</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">tl.to(".a", { x: 100 })
  .to(".b", { x: 100 }, "-=0.3")   // 0.3s pehle start (overlap)
  .to(".c", { x: 100 }, "+=0.2")   // 0.2s baad start (gap)
  .to(".d", { x: 100 }, 0)         // absolute 0-second mark
  .to(".e", { x: 100 }, "<")       // previous jaisa hi start time
  .to(".f", { x: 100 }, "myLabel"); // ek named label par start</code></pre>

  <pre><code class="language-javascript">tl.addLabel("start")
  .to(".a", { x: 100 })
  .addLabel("middle")
  .to(".b", { x: 100 })
  .to(".c", { opacity: 1 }, "middle"); // .c exactly .b ke start time par</code></pre>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Matlab</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>"+=1"</code></td><td>previous ke end ke 1 second baad (gap)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>"-=1"</code></td><td>previous ke end se 1 second pehle (overlap)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>0.5</code></td><td>absolute time, timeline ke start se 0.5s</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>"&lt;"</code></td><td>previous jaisa hi start time</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>"&lt;0.2"</code></td><td>previous start hone ke 0.2s baad</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>"myLabel"</code></td><td>ek named label par</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>2.5 Control methods aur playback</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">const tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });
tl.to(".box", { x: 300, duration: 1 });

tl.play();
tl.pause();
tl.reverse();
tl.restart();
tl.seek(0.5);        // 0.5 seconds par jump karo
tl.progress(0.5);     // 50% progress par jump karo
tl.timeScale(2);      // 2x speed par play karo
tl.timeScale(0.5);    // half speed par play karo</code></pre>

  <pre><code class="language-javascript">gsap.to(".box", {
  x: 300,
  onStart: () => console.log("started"),
  onUpdate: () => console.log("every frame"),
  onComplete: () => console.log("done"),
  onRepeat: () => console.log("looped again")
});</code></pre>

  <pre><code class="language-javascript">gsap.to(".loader", {
  rotation: 360,
  duration: 1,
  repeat: -1,        // -1 = infinite
  ease: "linear"
});

gsap.to(".pulse", {
  scale: 1.1,
  duration: 0.8,
  repeat: -1,
  yoyo: true,        // aage-peeche reverse
  ease: "sine.inOut"
});</code></pre>

  <h2>2.6 <code>gsap.set()</code>, defaults, aur global config</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">// Instantly styles apply karo, koi animation nahi
gsap.set(".card", { opacity: 0, y: 30 });

// Timeline-wide defaults, har child tween inherit karta hai
const tl = gsap.timeline({ defaults: { duration: 0.5, ease: "power2.out" } });

// Global config (kam hi chahiye hota hai)
gsap.config({ nullTargetWarn: false });
gsap.defaults({ ease: "power2.out", duration: 0.6 }); // pure app mein SAB tweens par apply</code></pre>

  <div class="practice">
    <div class="h">🎯 Practice — Part 2</div>
    <ol>
      <li>Ek timeline banao jo 3 boxes ko sequence mein animate kare, phir second tween ko <code>-=0.2</code> seconds early start karo.</li>
      <li>Ek timeline mein <code>"reveal"</code> label add karo, phir ek 4th tween ko exactly us label par start karo.</li>
      <li>12 grid items ko <code>grid: "auto", from: "center"</code> wale 2D stagger se animate karo. <code>from: "start"</code> se compare karo.</li>
      <li><code>repeat: -1</code> aur <code>ease: "linear"</code> use karke ek infinitely rotating loader banao.</li>
      <li>Ek paused timeline banao aur Play / Pause / Reverse buttons wire karo.</li>
    </ol>
